module gunbc.plans.fabric_serving_router

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn fabric_serving_router_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Goal: dashboard agent streaming OpenAI-compatible completions on flex-rented cards, Vast first/AWS later. Approved #14929; #14927 duplicate lane closed; slices have separate PRs. Operator 2026-10-23: ctrl is throwaway, no dependency on it or its request-count replica ranking. Evidence base cb6548946213 is dated."),
    p(text: "Contract: router_realization.router_capability_permission permits normalization→placement→granted endpoint→byte proxy→seat release. Never ComputeOwnLoadScore, SelectHostDirectly, authoritative binding ledger, FabricatePlacementWhenUnreadable or ForwardWithoutPermit. Reuse harness_place_cli/harness_release_cli, turn_admission, product.capacity lease/events/redemption and fabric.selection.select_supply; front_door admission/redeem/stream-end/recover own seats. rented_release owns drain/revoke/clean/destroy decisions; rented_allocation_host_enrollment derives enrollment, replacing the recorded empty hand list."),
    p(text: "Decided: upstream proxy carries bytes; NativeServeDriver callouts carry decisions. Do not extend seed gunbc serve (SeedFeatureCompletion/PublicSurfaceGrowth) or embed a handmade Rust relay in emitted main. NativeServeDriver already admits outgoing HTTP/clock, has a native-serve end-to-end instrument and approval_device_crypto_serve precedent. OpenAI wire belongs to extdeps.llm.openai/openai_contracts/openai_compat_sse/openai_errors/openai_rest, not a new extdeps.openai or OpenRouter key API."),
    p(text: "Pin the chosen Envoy/OpenResty upstream in extdeps and emit config from typed directives. Upstream comes ONLY from authz’s endpoint/permit; explicitly disable static upstreams, load balancing, retries and health routing, with controls. Authz unreachability or malformed admission refuses without forwarding. Authz normalizes/places/admits/redeems; stream-end calls front_door_stream_end then releases. Body bytes remain unchanged."),
    p(text: "S1/#14938 carries typed OpenResty directives and string-rendered nginx/Lua config under the 2026-10-24 operator scaffold ruling. Its tracking row must exist; this plan alone admits nothing. It dissolves into a native-emitted streaming door or earlier nginx/Lua grammar rows, never permanent Rust templates. Scratch inference favored OpenResty’s HTTP stream-end hook over Envoy’s gRPC sinks; it is not committed measurement. Adoption requires S1b before/with S1 and before S3; red reopens proxy choice/reverts S1, never waives proof."),
    p(text: "S1b/#15089: committed //gunbc/instruments:router-proxy-falsifier through native claim + extdeps.docker.cli_service.DockerCli on fleet (native_claim_route_admits_the_docker_cli ruling 2026-10-25). No daemon means no observation. Pinned proxy/emitted config must relay SSE before upstream end and report permit-bound stream-end on normal end, client abort and upstream reset; body reaches authz; refusal/unreachable/malformed answer forwards nothing; nginx -t passes and unknown-directive mutant reds. Planned candidate comparison uses streamed fake upstream/stub callouts; rerun against real S3 callouts."),
    p(text: "S2 extends only missing request readers (model/prompt size/stream). S3 emits serving_router as a separate srv1 NativeServeDriver unit, never inside roadmap_serve’s seed serial dashboard loop. Existing thread-per-connection request/response callouts need no door change. Call placement folds in-process, admit/redeem, test every RouterCapability arm. Before S3 lands, kill proxy mid-stream in a committed run and observe recovery by front_door_recover/lease expiry; failure reopens proxy selection."),
    p(text: "Warm sessions stay host-local/sticky through select_supply’s affinity rendezvous, never a router table. Cold prefill is measured acquisition cost on that fold; turn caps are admission policy and excess queues in turn_admission. Engine/cards/KV/throughput-by-active-turns/session-RAM profile belongs to serving measurements, not copied constants here."),
    p(text: "S4: pool key via request_authentication/serving_key_grant; tailnet-only TLS, no PR keys/endpoints. S5: durable enrollment from every live allocation after supplier-agnostic #14879; do not edit its rented_allocation/rented_release carriers while open. S6: model reclaimed-session re-placement at replica_endpoint_launch’s incarnation frontier BEFORE driver; next turn asks placement/pays cold prefill, never router failover or a replica-set fiction. Reclaim walks drain→revoke→clean→destroy, stopping at first refusal; destroy waits for #14879 target fix. S7: proxy/callout units through live_deploy.apply_legs/emit, not handwritten scripts."),
    p(text: "First live target, after destroy fix: Vast Apply on, $50 cap, at most two cards. Stream one dashboard chat session to a rented card, reclaim it, then place its next turn on the survivor. Red: any unpermitted served turn, seat held after stream end, or running rented card after reported reclaim completion."),
    p(text: "R — fabric-governed conversation relocation at turn boundaries. Operator ruling 2026-10-31: \"never move a session\" is the wrong invariant; the invariant is never LOSE or DUPLICATE a session's obligations while moving it. One operation moves an existing conversation to a selected replica for rebalancing, returned capacity, maintenance and recovery alike. Keep the current placement unless another admissible placement justifies its transition cost, or the current placement must be retired. Move between turns through a fenced, capacity-accounted handoff; a deliberate budgeted reconstruction is allowed, an unexpected cold re-read is not. Realized on the modeled router router_dev_policy as a manually invoked operation; its falsifier is //gunbc/instruments:router-proxy-falsifier, run on srv1 (v2-bootstrap runs no claim rows). NEVER implement movement by deleting nginx bindings or by touching the live hand-patched nginx on srv1 (~/router)."),
    p(text: "R reuse, do not re-mint: stay-versus-move is ONE product.fabric.selection.select_supply over candidates whose stateEstablishmentNames the transition-cost axis (a cold cache is a transition cost; unknown is distinct from none), with \"stay\" an explicit candidate carrying the incumbent's actual serving_session_standing/serving_session_residency, never its binding — a binding is not evidence of a warm cache and an unprobed owner pins the session, it does not relocate it. A conversation's long-lived retention reservation stays distinct from a turn's execution grant: retention is the conversation's, execution capacity is admitted per turn under serving_group_admission. The already-budgeted destination capacity rides ResourceBudgetPolicy/select_resource_budget_supply (a request-bound policy, explicitly not a pricing fallback); no pricing is fabricated. There is no Lua-local migration score and no second ledger: the handoff runs through existing reservations and fencing."),
    p(text: "R handoff, four phases through existing reservations and fencing: (1) Select produces a move intent naming the conversation, the current placement revision, the destination launch, the state-establishment method, the authorization and a bounded transition allowance; it deletes no binding. (2) Prepare, at the next turn boundary: serialize this conversation's dispatch, confirm the previous turn and its state finalization are finished, reserve destination retention at the conversation's declared growth allowance (not today's prompt size) plus execution capacity under the existing execution-class admission, and keep the source retention charged during the handoff. (3) Execute sends the next real client request ONCE to the destination — the authorized cold reconstruction, recorded as reconstruction and never advertised as a warm transfer; no speculative warm-up request. (4) Commit and retire, only after the destination completes and its retained-state standing is established: atomically advance the placement revision, record the destination launch and state, and retire the source reservation through its own authority. While a handoff is pending it is the one authoritative record; a competing request cannot pick either side; other conversations on the source are unaffected; returning to the source later is a new state-establishment decision on the now-current history, not a restore of the old binding."),
    p(text: "R state-establishment methods, two: restore_compatible_saved_state is a DECLARED method with no admitted case (no cross-engine KV transfer is established today), admitted only where compatibility and restoration are actually established; reconstruct_from_complete_request is the first realization, admitted only when the request carries everything needed to continue (history, tool definitions, tool results, reasoning and template settings, referenced inputs) and the destination satisfies the model and quality contract. Sharing a router alias is not evidence of either."),
    p(text: "R failure rules: before destination dispatch a failed preparation releases the temporary reservation and the original placement stands; a dispatch with an uncertain outcome recovers the recorded attempt and never blindly sends the turn elsewhere; once any response has been exposed that turn is never replayed on the old engine but becomes an explicit interrupted or recovery state; a controller restart reads the durable handoff and reconciles — a missing in-memory binding is neither a new conversation nor free capacity. The handoff record is durable on gunbc.serving.caller_backlog's rebinding spine (DurableRebindStanding, AttemptFence generations, predecessor checks), so a retried decision cannot move a session twice; placement revisions are recorded for the same reason."),
    p(text: "R policy: congestion may justify a move and a persistently overloaded replica may repay reconstruction, but a transient queue usually does not; prefer staying on a tie or an unsupported benefit and require an explicit margin; rate limits are rollout policy, not law; maintenance or retirement removes \"stay\" as a feasible candidate, and the question becomes which admissible transition satisfies the drain. First rollout uses the existing ResourceBudgetPolicy route: a commissioned owned-fleet relocation trial may spend one bounded reconstruction and one handoff's temporary overlap. Non-goals: cross-engine KV transfer, a fleet-wide optimizer, rental autoscaling, moving a batch sized by arithmetic (11 retained minus 4 slots is not 7 excess conversations), and predicting long-context reconstruction time from a short probe."),
    p(text: "R durability and its falsifier. The modeled router's Lua shared dict survives an nginx HUP but not a container restart, so router_dev_policy realizes only what a HUP-surviving dict can honestly carry, and a full container restart mid-handoff is an EXPLICIT TYPED REFUSAL in the realization: the conversation is refused, never treated as new and never double-dispatched. Its durable realization lands with this plan's S3 native serving_router unit. //gunbc/instruments:router-proxy-falsifier executes the real route with five cases, each red when its rule is removed (mutation stated): a successful move followed by warm continuations on the destination including a tool pause and competition from another admitted conversation (remove the commit-and-retire/revision-advance and the continuation reads the retired source); a failed destination preparation leaving the original placement intact (remove the pre-dispatch release-and-stand and a torn handoff strands the conversation); a racing request during the handoff (remove the pending-handoff-is-the-one-record fence and a competing request picks a side); a duplicate move command (remove the placement-revision/AttemptFence claim and a retried move moves twice); and a controller restart mid-handoff where an HUP reconciles while a container restart refuses and never double-dispatches (remove the restart-refusal and an unreconcilable handoff is read as a new conversation). Each proves capacity stays accounted and no request is ever forwarded to both replicas."),
  ]
}

data fabric_serving_router_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "fabric-serving-router",
  title: "Fabric-native serving router: proxy bytes, native-door decisions, OpenAI wire, rent-to-enroll and reclaim",
  body: fabric_serving_router_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this plan when S1 to S7 are realized and their rules are carried by the serving, proxy extdeps and live_deploy modules' own declarations and witnesses.") },
}
